 "labels": {
  "mode": "model alone: the megakernel feeds the model its own predictions; the reference only checks the stream afterwards (results/video_*.json). In the session, Qwen's replies are its own greedy tokens; the chat harness types the command from Qwen's tool call as keystrokes at record boundaries (call*_keys), the session's only inputs; the boot's only input is GO",
  "wrong": "tokens that differ from the reference machine's stream so far: 0 for every run (each stream's sha256 equals the reference's)",
  "speed": "real decode seconds per video second, per piece (segments)",
  "page square": "1 square = 4 KB of the machine's 4.5 MB of memory; lit = a store into it in this frame (fades over 0.5 s); free / in use / reserved from the kernel's struct page array, read from the machine's RAM",
  "register cell": "lit = the register was written in this frame",
  "heartbeat": "a pulse per timer interrupt (TRAP token, mcause 0x80000007)",
  "layer bar": "model.layers 0-36 (the CPU) glow while machine tokens decode, 37-68 (Qwen) while Qwen writes; a CPU layer flashes when the state it holds is written (registers: 4, privilege: 5, RAM: by address)",
  "zoom transitions": "dashed outlines are the zoom between levels (illustrative); every value shown is read from the snapshot",
  "crash block": "the sliding 512 KB outline is illustrative: each aligned 512 KB block shows its real count of free pages from struct page"
 },
